      "hints": [
        "Put over common denominator: $(\\cos\\theta-4)(5\\cos\\theta-2) - 4\\sin^2\\theta = 0$.",
        "Expand and replace $\\sin^2\\theta = 1 - \\cos^2\\theta$.",
        "Simplify: $9\\cos^2\\theta - 22\\cos\\theta + 4 = 0$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Combine the fractions over a common denominator and equate the numerator to zero:\n$$(\\cos\\theta - 4)(5\\cos\\theta - 2) - 4\\sin^2\\theta = 0$$",
        "Expand the first product and substitute $\\sin^2\\theta = 1 - \\cos^2\\theta$:\n$$5\\cos^2\\theta - 2\\cos\\theta - 20\\cos\\theta + 8 - 4(1 - \\cos^2\\theta) = 0$$\n$$5\\cos^2\\theta - 22\\cos\\theta + 8 - 4 + 4\\cos^2\\theta = 0$$",
        "Collect like terms to obtain the required quadratic in $\\cos\\theta$:\n$$9\\cos^2\\theta - 22\\cos\\theta + 4 = 0$$"
      ],
