      "hints": [
        "Solve quadratic for $\\cos\\theta = \\frac{22 \\pm \\sqrt{340}}{18} \\approx 0.1978$ (reject $2.247$).",
        "Find $\\theta = \\cos^{-1}(0.1978) \\approx 78.6^\\circ$.",
        "Find second solution $360^\\circ - 78.6^\\circ = 281.4^\\circ$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Solve the quadratic equation $9\\cos^2\\theta - 22\\cos\\theta + 4 = 0$ using the quadratic formula:\n$$\\cos\\theta = \\frac{22 \\pm \\sqrt{(-22)^2 - 4(9)(4)}}{2(9)} = \\frac{22 \\pm \\sqrt{340}}{18}$$\n$$\\cos\\theta = 2.247 \\quad (\\text{reject since } |\\cos\\theta| \\le 1) \\quad \\text{or} \\quad \\cos\\theta \\approx 0.1978$$",
        "Find the first quadrant solution for $\\theta$:\n$$\\theta_1 = \\cos^{-1}(0.1978) \\approx 78.59^\\circ \\approx 78.6^\\circ$$",
        "Find the fourth quadrant solution within $[0^\\circ, 360^\\circ]$:\n$$\\theta_2 = 360^\\circ - 78.59^\\circ = 281.41^\\circ \\approx 281.4^\\circ$$\n$$\\text{Solutions: } \\theta = 78.6^\\circ, \\quad 281.4^\\circ$$"
      ],
